Wings patch 0015: read pages that need JavaScript in web_fetch and research

Upstream's web_fetch returns nothing for pages that build their text with
JavaScript (single page apps, many news, shop and dashboard sites), and
deep research's browser fallback calls private_browser "read", which
upstream retired (it always answers page_unavailable), so research could
not read those pages at all. OpenManus reads them with a headless browser
(crawl4ai and browser-use).

  * src/agent_tools/web_tools.py: when the plain fetch got no text, an
    empty body, a bot challenge or HTTP 403, or only a JavaScript app's
    shell, web_fetch reads the page in the Wings renderer and says so.
  * src/research_navigator.py: the research browser fallback uses the
    renderer.

The renderer (wings/render.py, compose service `renderer`) is a stateless
copy of the browser container: no profile volume, so no logins, cookies or
downloads; a fresh browser context per read; its own network and secret,
so a hostile page there cannot reach the signed in browser. The browser's
URL rules and egress proxy (no private addresses) apply.

